#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:1
msgid "ADR-0015: Service layer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:5
msgid ""
"**Plan step**: P13.1 (REQ-SVC-1, REQ-MCP-5); the plan calls it "
"\"ADR-0007\", a number already used by \"Stochastic elements\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:8
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:10
msgid ""
"The web interface (phase 14) and the MCP server (phase 13) must offer the"
" same operations as the Python API, with the same results (objective O4)."
" Writing them twice would let them drift apart. Both also need safeguards"
" that the Python API leaves to the user: quotas, the gating of the "
"operation of equipment, errors that explain how to fix the request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:15
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:17
msgid ""
"`lumos.service.Service` is the single implementation of the high-level "
"operations: sessions (each with the origin of its actions, `python`, "
"`web` or `mcp`), contexts (create, presets, `.lumos` import and export, "
"Python export), editing (elements, connections, parameters, observation "
"band, processing chains), verification (validation with hints, "
"propagation plans), runs in a thread pool with progress, inspection of "
"ports (compact summaries and PNG figures), catalogues, archives and "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:22
msgid ""
"Inputs and outputs are Pydantic models (`lumos.service.models`); every "
"quantity is written as text with its unit (`\"0.5 mm\"`), parsed by "
"astropy (no evaluation of code)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:24
msgid ""
"Errors are `ServiceError` with a message, a hint (how to fix it) and a "
"code (`invalid`, `not_found`, `forbidden`, `quota`, `failed`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:26
msgid ""
"Safeguards in the service, whatever the adapter: quotas (contexts per "
"session, runs at a time, run duration); actions on equipment refused "
"unless the operation is enabled by the configuration and the call is "
"confirmed (`confirmed=True`, set by the adapter after asking a human); "
"the emergency stop is always allowed; archives are only read inside the "
"archive directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:30
msgid ""
"The web backend and the MCP server translate their protocol into these "
"calls and nothing else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:32
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:34
msgid ""
"Adapters calling the Python API directly: no parity by construction, "
"duplicated safeguards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:35
msgid ""
"An HTTP API used by the MCP server: an extra hop and a running server "
"even for local stdio use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:36
msgid ""
"asyncio throughout: the core is synchronous and CPU-bound; a thread pool "
"keeps the event loops of the adapters free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:39
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:41
msgid ""
"Each new feature of LUMOS reaches the web and the assistant once added to"
" the service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:42
msgid ""
"A context is not thread-safe: the service serialises the runs and edits "
"of a session with a lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0015-service-layer.md:43
msgid ""
"Presets are shipped in the wheel (`lumos/presets`) so that installed "
"servers have them."
msgstr ""

